          <span class="quote-mark">"</span>

          <h3>

            Compassion is not measured by how much we have,
            but by how willing we are to share what little
            we possess.

          </h3>

        </div>

      </div>

      <div class="journey-text">

        <span class="section-tag">

          A NEW DIRECTION

        </span>

        <h2>

          From Banking to Building Bridges of Hope

        </h2>

        <p>

          The encounter with the little street boy remained with Peter long
          after he drove away that day. He could not forget the generosity of
          a child who had almost nothing, yet freely offered the little he had.

        </p>

        <p>

          That moment became a turning point in his life. It challenged his
          understanding of success and inspired him to pursue a life dedicated
          to serving vulnerable children and communities.

        </p>

        <p>

          Peter made the courageous decision to leave the banking and finance
          industry and devote himself to humanitarian work. He founded
          <strong>Such As I Have Foundation</strong>, where he began working
          closely with children living in vulnerable circumstances and families
          facing significant challenges.

        </p>

        <p>

          His passion for compassion and community transformation later led
          him to join the <strong>Global Compassion Coalition (GCC)</strong>,
          an international movement connecting people who are committed to
          serving others through practical acts of compassion.

        </p>

        <p>

          Through the GCC Connectors Program, Peter met compassionate leaders
          from different parts of the world. Among them was <strong>Tinah</strong>,
          whose encouragement and friendship strengthened the growing vision of
          serving communities through collaboration rather than working alone.

        </p>

        <p>

          As his leadership and commitment continued to grow, Peter was
          entrusted with serving as the
          <strong>National Coordinator of the Global Compassion Coalition
          Connectors Program in Uganda</strong>, helping connect individuals,
          organizations and communities that share a common desire to transform
          lives through compassion.

        </p>

        <p>

          Along this journey, Peter was joined by many committed people who
          shared the same vision. Among them was
          <strong>Christine</strong>, whose passion for supporting vulnerable
          children, women and communities became an important part of the
          growing movement that would later become Compassion Bridge Initiative
          Uganda.

        </p>

      </div>

    </div>

  </div>

